# 301 redirect the old .org domain (any path, both bare and www) to the
# new .com site. Domain-qualified on the "from" side so this rule only
# fires when the incoming request's Host is brucesbreads.org -- it's a
# no-op on bruces-breads.com even though this same file, from this same
# repo, also gets deployed there via the Cloudflare Pages build.
#
# The trailing "!" forces the redirect even though this site has a real
# index.html/page at every one of these paths -- without it, Netlify's
# default "serve the matching file if one exists" behavior wins and the
# redirect never fires. That was the silent failure in the previous version.
https://brucesbreads.org/*      https://bruces-breads.com/:splat   301!
https://www.brucesbreads.org/*  https://bruces-breads.com/:splat   301!
